\n   - Chernov (blonde) \u2260 brunette (surname).  \n   - Ryzhov (brunette) \u2260 red (surname).  \n   - The brunette (Ryzhov) spoke to Belokurov, satisfying the interaction.  \n\nThis logical progression adheres to all given constraints.", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Set up the problem according to the given information:**\n\n   Three people are discussing - Belokurov, Chernov, and Ryzhev. Each of them has a hair color that does not match their surname: one is blond, one is brunette, and one is red-haired.\n\n2. **Translate the problem into constraints:**\n\n   Based on the given information, the following constraints can be derived:\n   - Belokurov is not blond.\n   - Chernov is not brunette.\n   - Ryzhev is not red-haired.\n   Additionally:\n   - Belokurov is also not brunette, since the brunette is speaking to Belokurov.\n\n3. **Create a table to assist in determining the correct hair colors:**\n   \n   Let's fill a 3x3 table with the surnames as rows and hair colors as columns. We'll use \"+\" to indicate a possible match and \"-\" to indicate an impossible match.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\n   \\hline\n   & \\text{Blond} & \\text{Brunette} & \\text{Red-haired} \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Belokurov} & - & - & + \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Chernov} & + & - & - \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Ryzhev} & + & + & - \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Analyze the table to deduce the hair colors:**\n\n   From the constraints:\n   - Since Belokurov cannot be blond or brunette, he must be red-haired. Place a \"+\" in the Belokurov row under the Red-haired column and \"-\" in the other cells of the same row.\n   \n   Update the table to:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\n   \\hline\n   & \\text{Blond} & \\text{Brunette} & \\text{Red-haired} \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Belokurov} & - & - & + \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Chernov} & + & - & - \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\text{Ryzhev} & + & + & - \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\