or in expanding the equations.\n\nSo now the equation is |Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p = 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2. Let's write this as:\n\n|Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p = 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2\n\nBut how can we interpret this equation? It relates Q and p. Since p is fixed, this is the equation of the locus of Q.\n\nLet me rearrange this equation. Let's write it as:\n\n|Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p - (3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2) = 0\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in Q. Let me try to complete the square or express it in terms of Q and p.\n\nLet me consider |Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p. Let's complete the square with respect to Q:\n\n|Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p = |Q - (p/2)|\u00b2 - |p/2|\u00b2\n\nBecause:\n\n|Q - (p/2)|\u00b2 = |Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p + |p/2|\u00b2\n\nTherefore,\n\n|Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p = |Q - p/2|\u00b2 - |p|\u00b2 / 4\n\nSubstituting into the equation:\n\n|Q - p/2|\u00b2 - |p|\u00b2 / 4 = 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2\n\nTherefore,\n\n|Q - p/2|\u00b2 = 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2 + |p|\u00b2 / 4\n\nSimplify the right side:\n\n3R\u00b2 - (2|p|\u00b2 - |p|\u00b2 / 4) = 3R\u00b2 - (8|p|\u00b2 / 4 - |p|\u00b2 / 4) = 3R\u00b2 - (7|p|\u00b2 / 4)\n\nWait, no:\n\nWait, 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2 + |p|\u00b2 / 4 = 3R\u00b2 - (2|p|\u00b2 - |p|\u00b2 / 4) = 3R\u00b2 - (8|p|\u00b2 / 4 - |p|\u00b2 / 4) = 3R\u00b2 - (7|p|\u00b2 / 4)\n\nWait, no. Wait, 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2 + |p|\u00b2 / 4 is equal to 3R\u00b2 - (2|p|\u00b2 - |p|\u00b2 / 4). Wait, actually, it's 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2 + (|p|\u00b2)/4 = 3R\u00b2 - (8|p|\u00b2)/4 + (|p|\u00b2)/4 = 3R\u00b2 - (7|p|\u00b2)/4.\n\nSo,\n\n|Q - p/2|\u00b2 = 3R\u00b2 - (7|p|\u00b2)/4\n\nTherefore, the locus of Q is a sphere centered at p/2 with radius sqrt(3R\u00b2 - (7|p|\u00b2)/4).\n\nBut wait, this seems a bit odd. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me retrace the steps:\n\nFrom |Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p = 3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u00b2\n\nThen, by completing the square:\n\n|Q - p/2|\u00b2 = |Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p + |p/2|\u00b2 = (|Q|\u00b2 - Q \u00b7 p) + |p|\u00b2 / 4 = (3R\u00b2 - 2|p|\u0