on 3:\n\nD - [ (v_g / v_m ) * (D + 8) ] = 8.\n\nCompute v_g / v_m:\n\nv_g / v_m = [ (D - 25)/(D + 25) ) / ( (D - 18)/(D + 18) ) ] = [ (D - 25)(D + 18) ] / [ (D + 25)(D - 18) ].\n\nTherefore, Equation 3 becomes:\n\nD - [ ( (D - 25)(D + 18) ) / ( (D + 25)(D - 18) ) ) * (D + 8) ] = 8.\n\nThis seems complex, but let's compute it step by step.\n\nLet me denote the fraction as:\n\n[(D - 25)(D + 18)] / [(D + 25)(D - 18)].\n\nMultiply that by (D + 8):\n\n[(D - 25)(D + 18)(D + 8)] / [(D + 25)(D - 18)].\n\nSo the equation is:\n\nD - [ ( (D - 25)(D + 18)(D + 8) ) / ( (D + 25)(D - 18) ) ) ] = 8.\n\nMultiply both sides by (D + 25)(D - 18) to eliminate the denominator:\n\nD*(D + 25)(D - 18) - (D - 25)(D + 18)(D + 8) = 8*(D + 25)(D - 18).\n\nNow, expand each term.\n\nFirst term: D*(D + 25)(D - 18)\n\nLet me compute (D + 25)(D - 18) first:\n\n= D^2 - 18D + 25D - 450\n\n= D^2 + 7D - 450.\n\nMultiply by D:\n\n= D^3 + 7D^2 - 450D.\n\nSecond term: (D - 25)(D + 18)(D + 8)\n\nFirst compute (D - 25)(D + 18):\n\n= D^2 + 18D -25D -450\n\n= D^2 -7D -450.\n\nThen multiply by (D + 8):\n\n= (D^2 -7D -450)(D + 8)\n\n= D^3 +8D^2 -7D^2 -56D -450D -3600\n\n= D^3 + (8D^2 -7D^2) + (-56D -450D) + (-3600)\n\n= D^3 + D^2 -506D -3600.\n\nThird term: 8*(D + 25)(D - 18)\n\nWhich is 8*(D^2 +7D -450) = 8D^2 +56D -3600.\n\nPutting all together:\n\nFirst term - second term = third term\n\nSo,\n\n[D^3 +7D^2 -450D] - [D^3 + D^2 -506D -3600] = 8D^2 +56D -3600.\n\nCompute left side:\n\nD^3 +7D^2 -450D -D^3 -D^2 +506D +3600\n\n= (D^3 - D^3) + (7D^2 - D^2) + (-450D +506D) +3600\n\n= 6D^2 +56D +3600.\n\nSet equal to right side:\n\n6D^2 +56D +3600 =8D^2 +56D -3600.\n\nSubtract left side from both sides:\n\n0 = 2D^2 -7200.\n\nTherefore,\n\n2D^2 = 7200\n\nD^2 = 3600\n\nD = 60 km.\n\nSince distance cannot be negative, D = 60 km.\n\nLet me check if this makes sense.\n\nSo D = 60 km.\n\nCheck Equation 1:\n\nv_m / v_k = (60 -18)/(60 +18) = 42/78 = 7/13 \u2248 0.538.\n\nEquation 2:\n\nv_g / v_k = (60 -25)/(60 +25) = 35/85 = 