e these ratios into Equation 3:\n     \\[\n     D - \\left( \\frac{(D - 25)(D + 18)}{(D + 25)(D - 18)} \\right)(D + 8) = 8\n     \\]\n   - Simplify and solve for \\( D \\):\n     \\[\n     2D^2 = 7200 \\implies D = 60 \\text{ km}\n     \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe distance from Zlatoust to Miass is \\(\\boxed{60}\\) kilometers.", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. Let the distance between the cities be $x$ km, and the speeds of the vehicles be:\n   - $\\text{GAZ}$: $g$ km/h\n   - $\\text{MAZ}$: $m$ km/h\n   - $\\text{KAMAZ}$: $k$ km/h\n\n2. We equate the time of travel for each pair of vehicles until their meeting points. This gives us the following equations based on the problem's information:\n   - $\\text{KAMAZ}$ meets $\\text{MAZ}$ at 18 km from Miass,\n   - $\\text{KAMAZ}$ meets $\\text{GAZ}$ at 25 km from Miass,\n   - $\\text{MAZ}$ meets $\\text{GAZ}$ at 8 km from Miass.\n\n3. Start by writing the equations for the times taken:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 18}{k} = \\frac{x - 18}{m} \\tag{1}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 25}{k} = \\frac{x - 25}{g} \\tag{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 8}{m} = \\frac{x - 8}{g} \\tag{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. Modify these equations to solve for the ratios by cross-multiplying:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 18}{x - 18} = \\frac{k}{m} \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 25}{x - 25} = \\frac{g}{k} \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 8}{x - 8} = \\frac{m}{g} \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n5. Multiply these three equations together:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{x + 18}{x - 18}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{x + 25}{x - 25}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{x + 8}{x - 8}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{k}{m}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{g}{k}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{m}{g}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n   Simplifying the right-hand side, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{k}{m} \\cdot \\frac{g}{k} \\cdot \\frac{m}{g} = 1\n   \\]\n\n   Hence, we obtain:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(x + 18)(x + 25)(x + 8)}{(x - 18)(x - 25)(x - 8)} = 1\n   \\]\n\n6. This implies:\n   \\[\n   (x + 18)(x + 25)(x + 8) = 